NAME
     paste - join lines side by side

SYNOPSIS
     paste [-s] [-d LIST] [FILE...]
     fold [-s] [-w WIDTH] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     paste writes the first line of every FILE as one line separated by
     tabs, then the second, and so on. Called as fold it breaks long
     lines instead.

OPTIONS
     -s        one file at a time: all of its lines on one line
     -d LIST   use these separators instead of tabs
     -w WIDTH  fold: break at WIDTH columns
     -s        fold: break at a space rather than mid-word

SEE ALSO
     cut(1), column layout in pr(1) is not provided
